Context
  Asked whether there is a standard location for Guile REPL logs and, if so, to
  add a monitors/monitors.json tailing it; then asked for a diagram of the
  surfaces (skills, agents, MCP, channels, communication styles) as a process for
  adding more, including the Emacs/Geiser + logs + debugging requirement.

  There is a standard location, so the monitor was straightforward. The diagram
  turned into docs/surfaces.org because the inventory was the interesting part:
  of about a dozen surfaces this plugin uses two.

Deviations
  The example in the request tailed the transcript equivalent (an application
  error log). This tails stderr instead, and says why in the script header. The
  transcript is the one file here that carries other people's input.

  `when: on-skill-invoke:guile-repl-server' rather than the default `always'. A
  monitor started in every session would tail a transcript directory in projects
  that never touch Guile.

Considerations
  The CLI validation gap is the real finding. Nine planted faults, all of which
  `claude plugin validate --strict' accepted, all of which validate-monitors.py
  rejects. Worth re-testing on a newer CLI: this is a measurement of one version,
  not a permanent property.

  Whether ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} and ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} are substituted into a
  monitor `command' is NOT verified here. The reference lists both as resolving in
  plugin configuration and forbids only ${user_config.*} in a monitor command, so
  the design follows the documented contract -- but the argument-handling branch
  for an unsubstituted literal exists precisely because it is unverified. Running
  it for real needs a session with the plugin loaded (gmake try).

  Stacked on fix/no-internal-endpoint-in-shipped-tree rather than branched from
  main, so plugin.json goes 0.1.5 -> 0.1.6 with no conflict. Per the version rule
  now in RELEASING.org: v0.1.4 is the highest published tag, PR #7 holds 0.1.5,
  so 0.1.6 is the next free number. Merge #7 first.

Clarifications
  docs/roadmap.org is referenced as plain text, not an org link: it lives on the
  other branch, and org-lint flags a link to a file that is not there yet.

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE, guile3 3.0.10, as dsp-dr. gmake checks
  green including the new check-monitors; validate --strict passing.
